      "body": "The S&P 500 closed Friday at 7,575 (+0.42%) and the Nasdaq-100 at 29,981 (+0.85%), both near record territory after a week of gains built partly on fading Iran war risk; that's now the rally facing its first real test when trading resumes Monday. Shipping and energy analysts had already flagged that owners remained wary of sending tankers back through Hormuz even during the calmer stretch, citing mine risk and elevated war-risk insurance costs — caution that looks prescient given Sunday's strikes.",
